const roadmap = `# Stoquify UI workflow implementation roadmap\n\n${stamp}\n\n**Decision:** execute all six proposals in the ${audit} and add two comparable, source-supported proposals: resumable new-PO authoring and reconciliation-alert processing recovery. This plan contains eight use cases and 20 delivery contracts. All packages are **PROPOSED**; publication does not mean implementation or release.\n\n## Outcomes and priority\n\n${planTable}\nP0 denotes an enabling or release gate, P1 the first value/operational-risk tier, and P2 the next tier. P2 still belongs in the committed scope. The ordering is a product hypothesis until UX00 measures actual task frequency and friction; a payroll cohort can legitimately prioritize UC03 ahead of search. UC07 and UC08 are completion work over existing foundations, not replacements for current PO editing or the durable inbox.\n\n## Delivery sequence and dependencies\n\n${table(['Wave','Work','Exit'],[
 ['0 — establish truth','UX00 → UX01','G0 baseline and G1 contracts, owners and decisions'],
 ['1 — useful read destination','UX02 → UX03; start UX04 once UX02 is ready','Item overview is independently pilotable; UX05 follows UX03 + UX04'],
 ['2 — high-value controlled workflows','UX06 → UX07; UX14 → UX15; UX16 → UX17','Payroll proof, new-PO recovery and alert diagnostics/recovery each pass their own gates'],
 ['3 — investigation and handoffs','UX08 → UX09; UX10 → UX11; UX12 → UX13','Communications, audit and access requests complete their role-specific tasks'],
 ['4 — integrated assurance and expansion','UX18 → UX19','All eight feature gates complete and accepted; operational ownership in place']])}\nWaves describe recommended sequencing, not mandatory serial execution. Independent feature lanes may overlap after UX01 when actual staff are available. Do not start UX05 until item/search destinations work. UX18 collects evidence continuously: its aggregate dependency list means all features must pass to close the program, not that an individual G4-complete feature must wait for all others to pilot. Apply the same per-feature interpretation to UX19; close the program only after every proposal passes.\n\n## Work package register\n\n${packageTable}\n**Estimate:** ${totals[0]}–${totals[1]} combined engineering/QA person-days, excluding specialist approval waiting, environment provisioning and elapsed pilot observation. These are initial planning ranges, not measured velocity or commitments. At 12–15 effective person-days/week, capacity arithmetic alone is approximately ${Math.ceil(totals[0]/15)}–${Math.ceil(totals[1]/12)} weeks; dependencies, staffing and review queues can lengthen this. Re-estimate after UX00/UX01 and after each first vertical slice. Owner labels are roles awaiting named assignment, not evidence that a team has accepted the work.\n\n## Decisions to record before dependent work\n\n${table(['Decision','Owner','Needed for','Default proposal / unresolved point'],[
 ['D01 cohort and task baselines','Product + QA','UX00','Choose representative stock, sales, purchasing, payroll and administrator users; baseline before claiming ROI.'],
 ['D02 customer search destination','Customer + IAM owners','UX04','Either respect existing read+analytics route authority or add a reviewed basic read profile; never widen grants silently.'],
 ['D03 eligible payroll evidence','Payroll + controls','UX06','Use already stored released register and approved provider/statement records; approve exact version/eligibility rules.'],
 ['D04 transport status mapping','Communication owner','UX08','Statements/invitations first; receipts conditional; accepted and unknown are not delivered.'],
 ['D05 audit projection and retention','Privacy + domain owners','UX10','Access/item fields first; no raw changes payload or exports; document event coverage.'],
 ['D06 access request operating policy','IAM + operations','UX12','Assign reviewers, expiry/SLA and application recovery; preserve decision versus effective grant distinction.'],
 ['D07 PO draft durability/retention','Purchasing + data owner','UX14','Durable scoped authoring drafts with explicit save/resume; define unsaved local-delta handling and retention.'],
 ['D08 alert recovery policy','Reconciliation + SRE','UX16/17','Diagnostic view first; explicit authorized retry only for eligible states; poison/lease failures escalate.'],
 ['D09 budgets and release exposure','Platform + QA + product','UX04 and releases','Propose ≤10 results/domain and p95 server search ≤750ms on agreed volume; validate before accepting as SLO.']])}\nA missing decision blocks the affected command/schema change, not unrelated source analysis or approved read-only slices. Record who decided, date, evidence and consequences. No decision has been silently accepted by the user merely because it appears here.\n\n## Coordinate with the existing platform roadmap\n\nThe separate ${link('platform roadmap','docs/prompt-execution/04_IMPLEMENTATION_ROADMAP.md')} contains R00–R37 and is preserved. These UX packages should be linked as children or acceptance slices of relevant parent work, not counted as duplicate delivery programs. Parent status must be checked before implementation; this table claims relevance, not parent completion.\n\n${table(['UI work','Existing parent packages','Integration rule'],[
 ['UX00/01/18/19','R00 baseline; R01 verification; R10 access; R24 EN/FR/accessibility; R31–R33 release/rollout','Share baseline, negative fixtures and release evidence; avoid separate certification claims.'],
 ['UC01/02','R11 master data; R12 inventory; R13 customer/order-to-cash; R14 purchasing','Reuse current entity truth and permissions; coordinate new read destinations.'],
 ['UC03','R17 payroll; R15 reconciliation; R07 close','Keep settlement controls and close invalidation authoritative.'],
 ['UC04','R22 customer/accountant delivery; R19 provider boundaries; R23 recovery','Expose source histories and existing recovery rather than introducing another sender.'],
 ['UC05/06','R10 access/privacy; R08 retention; R30 runbooks','Separate audit visibility, request decisions and actual permission grants.'],
 ['UC07','R14 purchasing/AP; R08 data/retention; R09 correction','Add authoring recovery without bypassing purchasing document controls.'],
 ['UC08','R15 reconciliation; R23 worker recovery; R30 operations','Add operator visibility and controlled commands over the existing inbox worker.']])}\n\n## Detailed delivery contracts\n\n${packages.map(p=>`### ${p.id} — ${p.title}\n\n**Status:** ${p.status}. **Priority:** ${p.priority}. **Owner:** ${p.owner}. **Effort:** ${p.effortPersonDays.join('–')} person-days. **Depends on:** ${p.dependencies.join(', ')||'none'}. **Use cases:** ${p.useCases.join(', ')||'shared foundation'}.\n\n**Current state:** ${p.currentState}\n\n**Objective:** ${p.objective}\n\n**Implementation locations:** ${p.paths.map(x=>'`'+x+'`').join('; ')}. Paths marked new are proposals; existing directories identify a discovery scope, not permission for a broad rewrite.\n\n**Implementation steps:**\n\n${p.tasks.map((s,i)=>`${i+1}. ${s}`).join('\n')}\n\n**Data and migration impact:** ${p.dataImpact}\n\n**Controls:** ${p.controls}\n\n**Verification:** ${p.verification}\n\n**Rollout and gate:** ${p.releaseGate}\n\n**Blockers and assumptions:** ${p.blockers}\n\n**Definition of done:** ${p.definitionOfDone}\n`).join('\n')}\n## Feature acceptance and value measurement\n\n${table(['Case','Minimum user acceptance','Metric to baseline'],cases.map(c=>[c[0],({UC01:'Reader answers item/stock questions without update authority; unknown never becomes zero.',UC02:'Exact and ambiguous references open the correct accessible destination; partial results are explicit.',UC03:'Controller selects eligible proof without a manual hash; invalid/replayed proof cannot settle twice.',UC04:'Operator finds a durable issue and reaches safe source recovery; accepted is not delivered.',UC05:'Auditor reconstructs the agreed scenario with safe fields and visible coverage limits.',UC06:'Request is tracked through decision and verified application; stale/self decisions cannot grant access.',UC07:'Saved new-order work resumes; commit-with-lost-response resolves to exactly one order.',UC08:'Operator diagnoses a stalled alert and retries only eligible work without stealing a lease.'})[c[0]],c[5]]))}\nUX00 owns baseline collection; domain owners review correctness; product compares pilot outcomes. A suggested task-time improvement target is 20% only if UX00 finds enough friction and sample size to justify it. It is not a forecast or release substitute. Report task success and error counts alongside time; faster incorrect completion is failure. Record denominators, role, dataset, language and environment. Use privacy-safe aggregate telemetry, never raw search text, employee proof or recipient tokens.\n\n## Verification commands and evidence policy\n\nExisting tests that are appropriate starting points (new behavior still needs dedicated tests):\n\n\`\`\`powershell\nnode node_modules/jest/bin/jest.js --runInBand --runTestsByPath components/purchase-orders/__tests__/purchase-order-edit-draft.test.ts services/payments/__tests__/payment-reconciliation-inbox-worker.service.test.ts\nnode node_modules/jest/bin/jest.js --runInBand --runTestsByPath config/__tests__/sidebar.test.ts components/dashboard/__tests__/DashboardRouteState.test.tsx services/payroll/__tests__/payroll-payment-reconciliation.service.test.ts services/users/__tests__/user-invitation-history.service.test.ts\n\`\`\`\nRun focused changed-boundary tests first, then typecheck and scoped lint as appropriate for implementation. Save command, exit code, revision, environment and failures without attributing existing failures to this work. New database concurrency and browser tests must be authored against real contracts; the commands above alone do not certify them. **Do not run generic npm build as a harmless check:** the inspected build script includes migration-related operations. Use the reviewed build/migration process for the release environment.\n\nEvidence for each package goes into a package-specific execution record with source diff, test results, role matrix, runtime identity, decision links and gate sign-off. The machine-readable ${link('work package registry','what-next/ui-workflow-roadmap/work-package-registry.json')} records this initial plan; update status only after evidence satisfies the package contract.\n\n## Rollback and stop conditions\n\nDisable the affected feature entry point/read endpoint or command exposure using the existing release mechanism. Recheck direct-route/action access, not only navigation. Preserve durable requests, drafts, audit events and idempotency results. Drain or pause affected recovery commands safely; do not reset live leases or drop tables as a feature rollback. Schema rollback requires its own reviewed data-preserving migration. Stop expansion on any tenant leak, unauthorized grant, duplicate order/settlement, stale-proof acceptance, lease theft, or misleading outcome state. Define numeric performance/error stop thresholds in D09 from baseline evidence.\n\n## First execution brief\n\nStart with UX00 and UX01, then implement UX02/UX03 as the first vertical slice. Revalidate current files and the parent roadmap, assign owners and fixture access, freeze the item read DTO and location/field permissions, add the reader destination and focused tests, then perform authorized/denied EN/FR browser tasks. Save the implementation diff and evidence. Do not start all eight user interfaces against speculative contracts. Continue the remaining lanes in the dependency order above once each entry gate is met.\n\n## Scope exclusions\n\nNo application feature was implemented by this roadmap run. No AI decision system, statutory formula change, provider activation, external send, bulk retry, generic approval platform, new search infrastructure or audit export is included. Existing POS recovery and PO edit recovery are foundations to retain. Expansion beyond the eight proposals requires a new evidenced user outcome and dependency assessment.\n`;
const refined = `${core}\n\n# Execution prompt: UI workflow roadmap\n\n## Mission\n\nTurn the six proposals in ${audit} into a comprehensive implementation roadmap and add two to five proposals only where current source supports comparable operational value. Execute the planning and publication work now; do not implement application features.\n\n## Review ownership\n\nApply architecture, backend/integration, database/migration, security/IAM/privacy, frontend/design systems, workflow/accessibility/localization, product, QA/release, SRE/performance and SaaS/adoption lenses. Activate inventory, purchasing/AP, payroll, reconciliation, audit/records, communication/provider, accounting-close and change-management lenses where touched. Legal/statutory rule changes and AI decisions are outside this scope. Review as one coordinated analysis; this instruction does not require spawning agents.\n\n## Evidence to inspect\n\nRead current route/components/services/actions/schema and focused tests referenced in the source audit; use graphify-out as an older discovery aid only. Inspect existing PO create/edit recovery and reconciliation inbox/dashboard contracts for additional candidates. Check docs/prompt-execution for overlapping parent work before writing artifacts. Preserve dirty-worktree changes and unrelated lint issues.\n\n## Execution checklist\n\n1. Classify current implementation, genuine gaps, uncertain evidence and deferred extensions.\n2. Carry forward all six original proposals, with explicit users, value and acceptance criteria.\n3. Add only source-supported proposals; distinguish missing functionality from completion of an existing system.\n4. Build individually reviewable packages with owners, dependencies, effort, concrete paths, data/migration impact, controls, tests, rollout, blockers and definition of done.\n5. Supply sequencing, decision register, risk register, parent roadmap crosswalk, metrics and a first execution brief.\n6. Verify dependency integrity and source links; publish five Markdown/PDF pairs with the existing docs-report-publisher.\n\n## Expected artifacts\n\nWrite the five numbered report pairs under docs/ui-workflow-roadmap and machine-readable evidence under what-next/ui-workflow-roadmap. Preserve the separate existing docs/prompt-execution publication. Include refined prompt, actual execution report, findings/risks, detailed roadmap and executive summary.\n\n## Verification commands\n\nUse the two focused PO edit-draft and reconciliation worker Jest suites to verify existing foundations; report results separately from historical audit tests. Validate all package dependencies, use-case coverage, source links, Markdown hashes and PDF signatures/page counts. Publish with node .agents/skills/docs-report-publisher/scripts/publish_reports.mjs ui-workflow-roadmap.\n\n## Risk controls and non-goals\n\nKeep tenant/location scope, current authority, module entitlement, server-owned proof, idempotency, lease safety and source-specific statuses. Never equate request approval with effective grant or alert processing with settlement. No production mutation, message sending, migration, provider activation or feature implementation is authorized by this planning task.\n\n## Success criteria\n\nEvery original proposal and each justified addition maps to concrete packages and acceptance checks; estimates have explicit uncertainty; unavailable authenticated/runtime evidence remains visible; published reports are readable and verified; existing platform reports remain byte-identical.\n\n## Next execution prompt\n\nImplement UX00/UX01 and the UX02/UX03 item-read vertical slice from the detailed roadmap. Revalidate current state, satisfy entry decisions, preserve unrelated work, and produce source/test/browser evidence before claiming the slice complete.\n`;
const execution = `# Roadmap planning execution report\n\n${stamp}\n\n## What was executed\n\nProduced an eight-proposal, 20-package implementation plan from the ${audit}. Preserved all six recommendations and added two evidence-supported completion proposals. Applied the prompt-architect, roadmap-publisher and docs-report-publisher workflow. Used the new docs/ui-workflow-roadmap destination because the normal folder already holds a separate platform roadmap.\n\nInspected the original audit/evidence, current PO create/edit flow and service boundary, reconciliation dashboard/inbox worker contracts, older discovery reports/graphs, existing parent roadmap headings and publication scripts. Graph node finance_paymentreconciliationworkbench_tsx (community 13) was a navigation aid; current source determined the finding. A few guessed filenames were corrected through discovery; a missing guessed path was not treated as proof of missing functionality.\n\n## Additional source findings\n\n- ModernCreatePurchaseOrderForm stores authoring in React/form state. ModernEditPurchaseOrderForm separately restores scoped session drafts and retains pending requests. The inspected create action/service does not expose an equivalent stable create-request recovery contract. This supports UC07 without claiming that PO editing lacks recovery or that duplicates have occurred.\n- The reconciliation worker tracks attempts, nextAttemptAt, last safe error and leases. The dashboard queue selects a reduced record projection and maps payload.status; DurableNotificationInbox does not expose those processing diagnostics. Worker DTOs include leaseToken and must not be passed wholesale to the browser. This supports UC08 without claiming the durable inbox is absent.\n\n## Checks actually run\n\n\`\`\`powershell\nnode node_modules/jest/bin/jest.js --runInBand --runTestsByPath services/payments/__tests__/payment-reconciliation-inbox-worker.service.test.ts components/purchase-orders/__tests__/purchase-order-edit-draft.test.ts\n\`\`\`\n**Result: 2 suites, 13 tests passed; exit code 0.** These tests cover existing foundation behavior with test doubles/pure logic. They do not exercise the proposed new PO authoring persistence or alert operator command. The original audit's 79 passes are historical evidence, not newly run tests or a combined 92-test run.\n\nNo application implementation, full typecheck/lint/build, live database migration, provider action, authenticated browser journey or production deployment was performed. Skills were consumed, not edited; skill-creation validation is not applicable.\n\n## Deliverables and publication evidence\n\nThe five numbered Markdown documents and their matching PDFs live in docs/ui-workflow-roadmap. The ${link('registry','what-next/ui-workflow-roadmap/work-package-registry.json')} contains 20 full contracts and eight use-case mappings. Publication validation is recorded in ${link('publication validation','what-next/ui-workflow-roadmap/publication-validation.json')}; consult that manifest for actual output checks rather than treating this description as a test result. Preserved-publication hashes record the unrelated ten files in docs/prompt-execution.\n\nWindows denied an initial parent-directory creation through apply_patch before any file was written. Narrowly escalated directory creation succeeded. Publication uses the existing local Markdown-to-PDF renderer, not a replacement toolchain.\n\n## Limitations\n\nThe originating audit scanned 163 page entries including 144 dashboard entries, but protected runtime inspection was unavailable. The present work adds targeted source analysis and planning, not an exhaustive visual reassessment. Effort, ranking and proposed metrics remain estimates until UX00/UX01. The runtime has not been independently tied to the inspected working tree. No legal, accounting, security, privacy, accessibility or release certification is claimed.\n`;
const findings = `# Execution findings and risks\n\n${stamp}\n\n## Findings register\n\nThe first six proposals inherit the detailed source anchors and limitations of the ${audit}. Their underlying foundations are partial: item editing and related views, page search, controlled settlement, source delivery histories, audit storage and grant administration already exist. The missing pieces are the specific user workflows described below.\n\n${table(['Case','Assessment','Evidence / limit'],cases.map(c=>[c[0],c[3],c[7]]))}\n\n### Additional proposal UC07 — resumable new PO authoring\n\n${link('Create form','components/purchase-orders/ModernCreatePurchaseOrderForm.tsx:125')} holds steps/lines/form values in component state; ${link('submission','components/purchase-orders/ModernCreatePurchaseOrderForm.tsx:338')} sends the create request without the observed edit-draft recovery contract. The ${link('new-page wrapper','app/[locale]/(dashboard)/dashboard/purchase-orders/new/page.tsx:12')} and ${link('create action','actions/purchaseOrderWorkflow/purchaseOrderSystemAction.ts:156')} lead to ${link('transactional create service','services/purchase-order/purchase-order.service.ts:525')}, which allocates a document number and creates the order. No stable replay-result lookup was found in this inspected path. This is a bounded finding, not proof that every upstream caller lacks duplication controls.\n\nBy contrast, ${link('existing edit form','components/purchase-orders/ModernEditPurchaseOrderForm.tsx:102')} restores scoped session drafts, persists pending requests and handles uncertain outcomes. The additional proposal therefore extends recovery to new authoring. Its value is reduced re-entry and safe resolution of a lost response after commit; incidence and financial impact have not been measured. See UX14/UX15 for durable draft, unique request fencing, payload hash, status lookup, migration and browser verification.\n\n### Additional proposal UC08 — alert processing diagnosis and recovery\n\nThe ${link('dashboard queue contract','services/reconciliation/payment-reconciliation-dashboard.service.ts:99')}, ${link('inbox query','services/reconciliation/payment-reconciliation-dashboard.service.ts:357')} and ${link('mapping','services/reconciliation/payment-reconciliation-dashboard.service.ts:425')} expose business alert information without the worker lifecycle. ${link('DurableNotificationInbox','components/finance/PaymentReconciliationWorkbench.tsx:1467')} renders recorded alerts without processing attempts, retry timing or a recovery command.\n\nThe ${link('existing worker projection','services/payments/payment-reconciliation-inbox-worker.service.ts:269')} already holds status, attempts, nextAttemptAt, safe error and a lease token. A separate redacted operator projection is essential. Value comes from shorter diagnosis and recovery of stalled alerts, with no change to financial settlement. UX16/UX17 reuse durable queue truth, protect active leases and route poison/redaction failures to escalation. This is distinct from UC04 outbound communications.\n\n## Risk and dependency register\n\n${table(['Risk','Impact','Required mitigation / owner','Gate'],[
 ['R-UI01 protected runtime unavailable','Source-correct design may fail real role/task journeys','QA obtains authorized synthetic fixtures and binds runtime to source revision','G0/G3'],
 ['R-UI02 already-changing working tree / parent overlap','Duplicate or conflicting implementation','Revalidate each package and link parent R work before editing; platform owner','G0'],
 ['R-UI03 destination permission mismatch','Search shows unusable links or leaks restricted data','D02 and scope before query/count; IAM/domain owner','G1/G2'],
 ['R-UI04 stale or client-provided proof','Incorrect payroll settlement or close evidence','Transactional server resolution with replay/version/SoD regressions; payroll owner','G2'],
 ['R-UI05 status conflation','Users mistake approval/acceptance/recording for completion','Separate decision/grant, delivery certainty and worker lifecycle; UX/domain owners','G1/G3'],
 ['R-UI06 sensitive audit/inbox payload','Employee/customer/lease secret disclosure','Allowlisted DTOs and negative-field assertions; privacy/security','G2'],
 ['R-UI07 ambiguous new-PO response','Duplicate orders or lost authoring','Durable draft plus atomic request-result fencing and recovery; purchasing/data','G2/G3'],
 ['R-UI08 unsafe recovery race','Lease theft, repeated poison processing or duplicate side effects','State eligibility, concurrency fence, idempotency and escalation; SRE','G2/G4'],
 ['R-UI09 orphaned queues','Requests/exceptions accumulate without business value','Named owner, response expectations and support runbook; product/operations','G0/G5'],
 ['R-UI10 optimistic capacity/ROI','Unrealistic deadlines or unproven value','Re-estimate after contracts; measure task baselines and cohort outcomes; product','G0/G5'],
 ['R-UI11 destructive rollback or retention ambiguity','Loss of draft/request history or excess personal data','Additive migrations, retention decisions and data-preserving rollback rehearsal; data owner','G2/G4']])}\n\n## Implemented, partial, missing, risky, blocked and deferred\n\n**Implemented foundations:** scoped domain services, source histories, PO edit draft helper, durable reconciliation inbox/worker and shared route-state primitives. **Partial user experiences:** all eight cases build on those foundations. **Missing in inspected scope:** the specific destinations, aggregators, selectors, request lifecycle and operator projections listed above. **Risky:** extending visibility without field-level scope; introducing retries without stable request/lease boundaries. **Blocked verification:** authenticated role/mobile/browser and real-database race/migration evidence. **Deferred:** payroll uploads, audit exports, financial audit event families beyond reviewed scope, receipt delivery adapter until recovery contract exists, sensitive search domains and bulk retries. Deferred extensions are not omissions of the eight accepted outcomes.\n\n## Review perspectives\n\nArchitecture preserves domain truth and coordinates parent work. Backend and database reviews own atomicity, replay, schema and bounded queries. Security/privacy own role/entity/location scope and field redaction. Frontend/workflow/localization/accessibility own task completion and robust states. QA/release own evidence and negative paths. SRE owns leases, observability and rollback. Product/adoption own demand, metrics and operational ownership. Inventory, purchasing, payroll, reconciliation, communications, audit and accounting-close lenses preserve their existing controls. Statutory/country-pack rule changes are not applicable because this plan changes no calculation or jurisdictional rule; qualified review is required if scope later changes. AI/model governance is not applicable because no model decisions or agent actions are introduced. SaaS packaging remains unchanged, while module entitlement remains enforced. No perspective is represented as an independent certification.\n`;
const summary = `# UI workflow roadmap — executive summary\n\n${stamp}\n\n**Scope: eight proposals, 20 executable work packages.** All six audit recommendations are retained. Two additions have current source evidence and comparable operational value: new purchase-order draft/retry recovery, and reconciliation alert processing diagnosis/recovery. The complete ${detail} defines implementation steps, owners, dependencies, migrations, controls, tests and completion gates.\n\n${table(['Proposal','Value','Delivery'],cases.map(c=>[`${c[0]} ${c[1]}`,c[4],c[6]]))}\n\n## Recommended start\n\nAssign owners and establish baseline/contract evidence through UX00 and UX01, then deliver the read-only item workspace (UX02/03). It fixes a concrete missing destination and enables business-record search (UX04/05). Payroll guidance, PO authoring recovery and alert diagnostics can proceed as separate lanes after their contracts are approved. Communications, audit and access requests follow with their own source permissions and operational owners.\n\nEach completed feature can pilot after its own G4 evidence; the program closes only when all eight have passed integration and operational acceptance. Existing platform roadmap R00–R37 remains separate and unchanged; the detailed roadmap identifies overlapping parent work to avoid duplicate implementation.\n\n## Capacity and decisions\n\nInitial estimate: **${totals[0]}–${totals[1]} combined engineering/QA person-days**. Capacity arithmetic at 12–15 effective days/week is roughly ${Math.ceil(totals[0]/15)}–${Math.ceil(totals[1]/12)} weeks before external review, environment setup and pilot waiting; this is not a date commitment. Re-estimate after UX00/01. Decide customer search destinations, payroll proof eligibility, channel meanings, audit fields, access-review ownership, draft retention and alert retry authority before dependent work.\n\n## Evidence and release limits\n\nThis planning run passed **13 existing tests across two suites** for PO edit-draft and reconciliation worker foundations. The earlier audit’s 79 passes remain historical. No new feature, migration, live provider action or authenticated end-to-end workflow was implemented or verified. Protected role/browser access remains a release-evidence dependency.\n\nSuccess means faster correct task completion, safe recovery and clear ownership—not just eight new screens. Baseline time, success, error and recovery metrics first. Keep all existing settlement, permission, idempotency and lease controls. Release gradually and disable affected exposure on any critical correctness or disclosure failure while preserving durable history.\n\n## Published package\n\n1. ${link('Refined execution prompt','docs/ui-workflow-roadmap/01_REFINED_PROMPT.md')}\n2. ${link('Actual planning execution report','docs/ui-workflow-roadmap/02_EXECUTION_REPORT.md')}\n3. ${link('Findings and risks','docs/ui-workflow-roadmap/03_EXECUTION_FINDINGS_AND_RISKS.md')}\n4. ${detail}\n5. This executive summary.\n\nEvery Markdown report has a matching PDF. ${link('Publication validation','what-next/ui-workflow-roadmap/publication-validation.json')} records actual artifact checks; ${link('package registry','what-next/ui-workflow-roadmap/work-package-registry.json')} supports tracking and future execution.\n`;
const docs = {'01_REFINED_PROMPT.md':refined,'02_EXECUTION_REPORT.md':execution,'03_EXECUTION_FINDINGS_AND_RISKS.md':findings,'04_IMPLEMENTATION_ROADMAP.md':roadmap,'05_ROADMAP_EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY.md':summary};
for (const [file,content] of Object.entries(docs)) fs.writeFileSync(path.join(out,file),content);
fs.writeFileSync(path.join(evidence,'source-hashes.json'),JSON.stringify(Object.fromEntries(Object.keys(docs).map(f=>[f,hash(path.join(out,f))])),null,2));
console.log(JSON.stringify({documents:Object.keys(docs),packages:packages.length,useCases:cases.length,totalPersonDays:totals,preservedFiles:Object.keys(oldHashes).length}));
